SNAKE - 3270 fullscreen game
.sp
.il 3
The game of SNAKE is played on a board (screen) covered with numbers
in a range which depends on the size of the board, usually in the range
1..n, where n is from 5..9, smallest screen to largest screen. There is
a CURSOR, otherwise known as the HEAD of the SNAKE, which is represented
by a highlighted '*' with the terminal cursor '_' under it. The starting
position of the cursor is random as are the values placed in every cell
on the board.
.sp
.il 3
The object of the game is to 'eat' as many cells on the board as
possible, thus enlarging the SNAKE represented by a trail of '.' without
overstepping the '.'s and with as few bumps into the side as possible.
.sp
.il 3
Movement is accomplished by hitting the appropriate PFkeys which will
move in one of eight directions:
.sp
.fo off
        PF1,13  UL           PF2,14  U          PF3,15  UR
        PF4,16  L                               PF6,18  R
        PF7,19  DL           PF8,20  D          PF9,21  DR
.fo on
.sp
The number of cells to move is taken from the first cell in the
selected direction of motion. When the HEAD bumps into the side the
alarm will sound on those terminals that have alarms, the "STATUS"
area in the lower right hand corner will be highlighted, and the
BUMP value on the status line will be incremented by the number of
cells that could not be eaten, or by the highest number on the screen
plus one if the stupid SNAKE tried to move into a wall it could plainly
see. The EAT value on the status line will be incremented each time
the SNAKE manages to chomp a cell. The RANK will indicate the current
rank this SNAKE is now awarded based on how much of the screen he has
EATen and how many BUMP points he has scored (every 30 BUMP points cause
a reduction in one RANK).
.sp
.il 3
If at any time you wish to stop playing you may strike PA1, The word
'**END**' will appear in the STATUS area, and the game will terminate
upon any interrupt key being depressed.
If you want to pause in the game and come back some other time you
should press PF5 to save the current game on disk, to return to an old
game press PA2. CLEAR will return you to the current state of the game
after clearing the screen.
.sp
.il 3
The so called "STATUS" in the lower right hand
corner usually has rubbish in it, but sometimes there are important things
in it as follows:
.sp
.of 9
**END**  means the end of game has been reached, either by
the SNAKE who tried to eat himself, or by the user who struck
PA1, or when the SNAKE has managed to DEVOUR!! the entire board.
.of 9
SAVED    means that the current game board and all values
associated with it will be saved on disk for future RESTORation.
.of 9
RESTORED means that a game that was previously SAVEd has been
restored.
.of 9
WRONGCRT means that an attempt was made to restore a game that was
played previously on a different model 3270.
.of 9
$ERR ### means that an error code of ### was returned from some
CMS macro or another.
.of
.sp
.il 3
This game will work on all 3277, 3278 models 1,2,2A,3,4,5.
.sp
.fo off
    Written for your enjoyment by Yossie Silverman, W.I.C.C, Israel.
.fo on
